# Per-Dockerfile ignore override for web/Dockerfile (BuildKit's
# "<dockerfile>.dockerignore takes precedence over the root .dockerignore"
# convention), the same mechanism render-service/Dockerfile.dockerignore uses.
#
# This file is NOT optional here. The root .dockerignore excludes `web`
# outright — correct for the PHP image, which serves no frontend, and fatal for
# this one: without the override the build fails on a COPY of a directory that
# plainly exists in the checkout, which reads as a broken Dockerfile rather than
# as an ignore rule.
#
# Starts from `*` and re-includes, because this image needs a different slice of
# the monorepo than the PHP core image and gets its own ruleset rather than
# holes punched in that one. Re-including a nested path after an
# exclude-everything `*` requires re-including EVERY ancestor directory one
# level at a time (the same limitation .gitignore has).

*

# The workspace root. A single lockfile governs every workspace, so `npm ci`
# can only run from here.
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# The frontend itself. node_modules and .next are rebuilt inside the image —
# copying the host's would drag in host-arch binaries and a stale build, and
# they dwarf the source they would ship alongside.
!web
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/storybook-static
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# The workspace packages web imports. @amroksaleh/ui is consumed as SOURCE
# (next.config.ts transpilePackages) — there is no prebuilt artifact to copy, so
# the whole package tree has to be here.
!packages
packages/*/node_modules
packages/*/storybook-static

# npm validates the lockfile against EVERY workspace the root package.json
# declares, so each template's manifest has to exist or `npm ci` refuses to
# install. Nothing else under templates/ is part of this build — and
# src-tauri/target alone is a multi-gigabyte Rust build directory that would
# otherwise be uploaded as build context.
!templates
templates/*
!templates/*/package.json
